<title>USA: Alberto-Culver unit buys more UK stores.</title>
<headline>Alberto-Culver unit buys more UK stores.</headline>
<dateline>MELROSE PARK, Ill 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alberto-Culver Co said on Tuesday that a unit of its Sally Beauty Supply company has bought the Embassy Ltd beauty supply stores in Britain from Ascot Holdings.</p>
<p>The chain consists of 30 stores and was bought for $8 million, the company said. The chain operates primarily in the Midlands area and has sales of about $20 million.</p>
<p>Alberto-Culver said this brings the number of Sally's stores in Britain to 92 and enhances Sally's position as a large distributor of professional beauty supplies in Great Britain.</p>
<p>The Embassy stores will carry the Sally Beauty Supply name, Alberto-Culver said.</p>
</text>
